# Measure Value Objects

Measures are modelled as value objects: `Weight`, `Length`, `Volume` (`src/shared/`) and
`LoadingMeters` (`src/cargo-plans/ldm/`). They exist so that every calculation on a measure
lives in exactly one place.

## Rule: compute with the value object, never with its number

Domain and application code must not unwrap a measure (`valueInKg`, `valueInMm`, `valueInLdm`,
`valueInLitres`, `valueInUnit`) to add, compare, sum or pick extremes. If the operation is
missing, **add it to the value object** (with a cucumber scenario) instead of doing it inline.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD – a domain rule computed on raw numbers
const payload = Weight.from(Math.min(...members.map(m => m.payloadCapacity.valueInKg)), 'KG');
if (spec.width.valueInMm > loadSpace.width.valueInMm) { ... }
row.units.reduce((sum, u) => sum + u.weightKg + u.tareWeightKg, 0);

// ✅ GOOD – the value object owns the operation
const payload = Weight.min(members.map(m => m.payloadCapacity));
if (spec.width.exceeds(loadSpace.width)) { ... }
Weight.sum(units.map(u => spec.grossWeightOf(u.weight)));
```

## Rule: a domain formula is written once

A formula combining measures (gross weight = cargo + tare, total height = pallet base + cargo)
belongs to the domain object that owns it (`PalletSpec.grossWeightOf`, `PalletSpec.totalHeightWith`).
Projections and read models **call** it – they never re-derive it.

## Where unwrapping is allowed

Only at the edges, where the outside world speaks numbers:

- persistence: `*.repository.ts`, `in-memory/`
- read side: `*.queries.ts`, `*.readmodel.ts`
- HTTP boundary: `*.routes.ts`, `*.validation.ts`
- error construction: `new XxxError(actual.valueInKg, max.valueInKg)` – wording a message
- the measure value objects themselves

## Enforcement

`src/architecture/domain-arithmetic.feature` scans `src/cargo-plans` and fails on any unwrapped
measure or `Math.min`/`Math.max` outside the places listed above. It runs with
`npm run test:cucumber`. If it fails, move the logic into the value object; do not widen the
allow-list in the step definitions without a reason stated in the code.
